--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Description:
libnvv4lconvert.so is the DeepStream build of libv4lconvert (from v4l-utils).
It converts capture pixel formats. libnvv4l2.so links against it, and the
gst-v4l2 plugin (nvv4l2decoder) uses libnvv4l2.

Build this library before libv4l2. See ../README for the full order.

The library sources are LGPL-2.1-or-later. This README is Apache-2.0.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Platform:
x86_64 only. The Makefile stops on any other architecture, including Jetson.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pre-requisites:
- DeepStream SDK installed, so the install directory exists
- gcc

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Compiling and installing the library (from this directory):

  $ make && sudo make install

Skip sudo when already root (for example inside a container).

The default install directory is /opt/nvidia/deepstream/deepstream/lib/.
make install copies libnvv4lconvert.so there and adds a libv4lconvert.so.0
symlink to it.

To install somewhere else:

  $ make install LIB_INSTALL_DIR=<dir>/

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Verify:

  $ ldd /opt/nvidia/deepstream/deepstream/lib/libnvv4lconvert.so

After libv4l2 and gst-v4l2 are also installed:

  $ gst-inspect-1.0 nvv4l2decoder
